     "resume": "On 11 May 2026 the ICO fined South Staffordshire Plc and South Staffordshire Water Plc GBP 963,900 after an attack that exposed the data of 633,887 people on the dark web. The ICO found weak access controls, monitoring covering only 5% of the IT estate (intrusion undetected for ~20 months), obsolete software (Windows Server 2003) and poor vulnerability management; a 40% reduction was granted for cooperation."
